        "# H3 Infinite — Continuation Workflow\n\nUse this workflow for **Clip 2 and every later clip**.\n\n1. Set **Load Previous AV Latent** to the clip index saved by the previous run.\n2. Load the next **Last Frame** and optional `<Picture 1>` reference image.\n3. Enter the next action/dialogue prompt in **Continue from Latent v1.2**.\n4. Keep `handover_mode = auto`, `alignment_mode = phase_aligned_extended`, and `context_frames = 22` for the recommended path.\n5. Queue the workflow. Motion and native audio history are injected directly from the previous AV latent.\n6. Save the new latent under the next clip index and repeat.\n\nUse `Stitch Ready` when another clip follows. For the **last segment of the finished video**, use `Final Clip`: it removes the reused head overlap but preserves the complete final-keyframe landing.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#1f4d3b",
      "bgcolor": "#2c6b52"
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -930,
        40
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Models & optimization",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Model setup\nUse the **same H3 diffusion model, Qwen encoder, Video VAE, Audio VAE and resolution** as the previous clip.\n\nSageAttention is optional. Changing core model/VAE settings between clips can break continuity or latent compatibility.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1550,
        800
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Load previous latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Load Previous AV Latent\nLoads the full sampler-output **video + audio latent** and the handover metadata saved by the previous clip.\n\nSet `clip_index` to the previous clip (for example `1` when generating Clip 2). The continuation node consumes the loaded latent directly — no decode/re-encode handover is used.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1080,
        990
      ],
      "size": [
        720,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 25,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Target / reference images",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Image inputs\n**Last Frame** is the target endpoint for this new clip.  \n**Reference Image** is optional Qwen guidance addressed as `<Picture 1>`.\n\nYou do **not** need to supply the previous clip's last rendered frame: temporal history comes from the previous AV latent.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -240,
        1080
      ],
      "size": [
        680,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 26,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Continue from Latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Recommended continuation settings\n- `context_frames = 22`: requested minimum motion/audio history.\n- `handover_mode = auto`: use analyzer metadata.\n- `alignment_mode = phase_aligned_extended`: recommended; preserves a late cutoff but extends history backward to a canonical H3 phase.\n- `manual_landing_tail_frames`: only relevant to manual/fallback operation.\n\n`actual_head_context_frames` can be larger than 22. Connect that output to **Output / Stitch** so the exact reused overlap is removed from the rendered continuation.\n\n\n**Prompting tip:** describe the action as continuing through the segment (for example `she continues walking`) rather than strongly instructing the model to settle into the Last Frame. Keep important dialogue away from the very end of a segment, where trimming may occur.\n\nIf unwanted background music is a problem, try appending `non_diegetic_music: N/A`. When using `<Picture 1>` for identity, explicitly describe it as the reference for the subject's facial features, clothing and body composition."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        390,
        830
      ],
      "size": [
        770,
        310
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 27,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Sampling settings",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Sampling\nUse the same sampler, scheduler, Sigma Shift and general H3 settings as the first clip unless you have a specific reason to change them.\n\nThe seed may be randomized per clip; continuity comes from the direct latent context and endpoint conditioning, not from reusing the same noise seed.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1580,
        1020
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        350
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 28,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Auto Handover",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Auto Handover\nAnalyzes the new clip so it can itself become the source for the **next** continuation.\n\n`Balanced` is the validated default. `Motion Safe` uses a more conservative safety margin. If no end freeze is found, the no-lock fallback excludes the final `freeze_hold - 1` frames before phase alignment.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1230,
        790
      ],
      "size": [
        350,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 29,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Save next AV Latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Save the next full AV latent\nSave the sampler's complete video + audio latent together with Auto Handover **and `actual_head_context_frames`**. The Save node stores that head length in the `.safetensors` metadata so the clip can later be stitched automatically without reopening this generation graph.\n\nKeep one numbered prefix (`clip_00001`, `clip_00002`, …) for the whole chain.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2030,
        560
      ],
      "size": [
        850,
        360
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 30,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Output / Stitch modes",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Output / Stitch\nFor Clip 2+, choose the mode based on what happens next:\n\n**Stitch Ready** — use when another clip follows. It removes both `actual_head_context_frames` from the beginning and the tail after the effective handover cutoff.\n\n**Final Clip** — use on the last segment. It removes the reused head overlap but keeps the complete tail, including the final Last Frame landing.\n\n**Full** — no trimming at all; mainly useful for inspection/debugging.\n\nVideo and audio always use the same trim range. If you later extend a chain, change the previous `Final Clip` back to `Stitch Ready`.\n\n\nFor the smoothest final joins, use the **3-Clip Showcase** or the separate **04 — Stitch Saved Chain** workflow. Those use the retained full context for Safe Tail Bridge, a short context-aligned video blend and a 15 ms audio de-click crossfade instead of a hard concatenation.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#66511f",
      "bgcolor": "#8a6d28"
    }
